--EXPECT--
```nvs
Core\Json::encode(mixed $value, {pretty?: bool, escapeUnicode?: bool} $options): string
```

Serializes `$value` as JSON text. It can be a scalar, an array, an anonymous object or an instance of a class with `#[Json\Derive]`. The text is on one line unless `pretty` is set.

**Parameters**

- `$value` — The value to encode: `null`, `bool`, `int`, `uint`, `float`, `decimal`, `string`, an array, a `{name: value}` shape, or an instance of a class carrying `#[Json\Derive]`.
- `pretty` — Indent the output across lines, as `JSON_PRETTY_PRINT` does; the default is one line.
- `escapeUnicode` — Write every non-ASCII character as a `\uXXXX` escape, as `json_encode` does by default; the default here keeps UTF-8 as it is.

**Returns** The JSON text.

**Throws**

- `LogicError` — `$value` holds something JSON cannot spell: a `NaN` or infinite `float`, a value of a type with no JSON encoding, an instance of a class without `#[Json\Derive]`, or nesting past 1024 levels.
